comments.body:
@Skeletor-Pirate it’s not about what I prefer. This is an OWASP community project, and all contributors need to follow our [Contributing Guide](https://github.com/OWASP/CheatSheetSeries/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md). We don’t accept PRs unless the issue is assigned to you, except for typo fixes, broken links, or minor adjustments to existing cheat sheets.

I’ve assigned this issue to @bhushan4work and @Skeletor-Pirate and reopened #2904. To avoid overlap:

@Skeletor-Pirate: XXE / entity expansion section (#2904)
@bhushan4work: malformed document and jumbo payload guidance
Schema validation stays with @Richa-techhub until Nov 10, as mentioned above.

Please keep PRs small (one section each) and review each other’s PRs.

@saxamkeshvani123456-maker sorry we missed your offer. There are other issues labeled HELP_WANTED if you’d like to pick one up.

Thanks @mackowski for clearing the split and for reopening #2904 — and understood on the contributing guide; with the assignment in place this follows it now.

Scope confirmation: the branch touches only the XML Security sheet's entity-expansion section, plus one regenerated line in Index.md (the Java language badge disappears along with the removed Java samples, which is what the earlier check run flagged). Markdownlint, textlint, citations, link-check and scope all passed in that run; the Index.md fix is pushed as 0bd44f4 and just needs the usual fork-run approval.

@bhushan4work whenever your malformed-document / jumbo-payload PR is up, ping me and I'll review it — per the above, one small section each, so those reviews should be quick for both of us.
